  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prevention Violent Extremism TJK</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is designed to address the urgent need for increased investment in prevention and resilience, solidarity, and a renewed social contract, as highlighted in the UNDP 2022 Special Report on Human Security. It adopts a people-centered, context-specific, and prevention-oriented approach to build community resilience, empower youth, and prevent violent extremism while strengthening social cohesion in Central Asia.Building on the successful outcomes of the 2018-2021 project at the community level, the project aims to expand national capacities in the prevention of violent extremism. It recognizes the importance of triggering positive change at multiple levels to effectively address the complex challenge of violent extremism.</narrative>
  </description>
